# Tests Required Before Staging

**No ticket can be submitted to staging without full automated tests written and passing.**

## Requirements

1. Every ticket fix MUST have at least one automated test file covering the fix
2. Tests MUST pass locally before the ticket can be deployed to staging
3. Test files go in `frontend/e2e/tests/regression/` named `ticket-{number}-{description}.test.ts`
4. Tests must make real assertions about specific values — not just status code checks

## Pre-Deploy Verification

Before running staging deploy commands, verify:

```bash
# Run all ticket regression tests
cd Frontend && npx jest --testPathPatterns="e2e/tests/regression/ticket-"
```

If any test fails, fix the issue before deploying. Never deploy untested code to staging.

## What Counts as "Full Tests"

- Backend logic changes: test the API endpoint behavior (correct response, error cases)
- Frontend UI changes: test that components render correctly, user interactions work
- State machine changes: test valid transitions succeed and invalid ones are rejected
- Validation changes: test both valid and invalid inputs
